# Executor-owed, BOX-LOCAL artefacts. ⛔ Never committed: PINNED_SRC_REV is the
# pin THIS BOX made after ITS bundle sync, and SRC_CLEAN.jsonl / SELFTEST_*.json
# / SMOKE_*.json / FPU_BITEXACT_LADDER.json are that box's own launch ledger.
# A committed pin would let one box's rev masquerade as the other's — the exact
# IS-A1 confusion `cross_box_rev_gate` exists to refuse — and a committed golden
# gate would let one box's WHEEL masquerade as the other's, which is the same
# defect one layer down (`carc_rs_binary_sha` is BOX-LOCAL: two boxes compiling
# identical source produce different bytes).
#
# ⚠️⚠️ EVERY PATTERN IS ANCHORED WITH A LEADING `/`. An unanchored
# `PINNED_SRC_REV` matches at ANY DEPTH and therefore swallows
# `selftest_fixture/PINNED_SRC_REV` — which is a COMMITTED FIXTURE FILE (the
# synthetic 40-hex pin `aaaa…` that `analyze_ladder.py --selftest` reads to
# exercise `cross_box_rev_gate`). Without it the selftest raises on a fresh
# clone, which would make the launcher's precondition ladder fail on every box
# that had not run make_fixture.py first. (Inherited verbatim from
# fpu_resurrection_prep, where it was learned the hard way.)
/PINNED_SRC_REV
/SRC_CLEAN.jsonl
/SELFTEST_*.json
/SMOKE_*.json
/FPU_BITEXACT_LADDER.json
/BAND_CLAIMED
/logs/
/__pycache__/
# the golden gate's six raw legs, copied beside its runner for by-hand review
/golden_gate/OLD.json
/golden_gate/NEW.json
/golden_gate/CTRL_*.json
/golden_gate/__pycache__/
